Link file_engine.o into the detection objects

With --enable-plugins --default-dynamic the scumm engine becomes
plugins/libscumm.so while the detection objects link into the main
scummvm binary. DETECT_OBJS picks up file.o and file_nes.o but not
file_engine.o, so ScummPAKFile - implemented there - has its vtable
emitted only inside the plugin.

engines/scumm/file.h gives ScummPAKFile an inline virtual destructor,
and detection.cpp includes that header. detection_internal.h deletes
through a BaseScummFile*, and at -O3 gcc speculatively devirtualizes
that polymorphic delete against the derived types it can see. That
emits ScummPAKFile's inline dtor into detection.o, which then
references a vtable the main binary does not have:

  engines/scumm/detection.o: in function `Scumm::ScummPAKFile::~ScummPAKFile()':
  undefined reference to `vtable for Scumm::ScummPAKFile'
  undefined reference to `VTT for Scumm::ScummPAKFile'

Whether gcc emits that dtor depends on per-target devirtualization
heuristics, so the failure is architecture-dependent - riscv64 hit it
while most other targets did not.

Add file_engine.o alongside its two siblings, which are already listed
here for the same reason. All three are in MODULE_OBJS as well, and
file_engine.cpp only reads ScummEngine members (_game.platform,
_containerFile, _game.id), so it pulls no engine code into the
detection library. The existing STATIC_PLUGIN guard still applies: a
static module already contains these objects.

Signed-off-by: Carlos Martins <cjom@reglinux.org>

diff --git a/engines/scumm/module.mk b/engines/scumm/module.mk
--- a/engines/scumm/module.mk
+++ b/engines/scumm/module.mk
@@ -289,5 +289,6 @@
 # module is enabled, because it already has the contents.
 ifneq ($(ENABLE_SCUMM), STATIC_PLUGIN)
 DETECT_OBJS += $(MODULE)/file.o
+DETECT_OBJS += $(MODULE)/file_engine.o
 DETECT_OBJS += $(MODULE)/file_nes.o
 endif
